    "https://www.sabanciuniv.edu/en/academic/support-education-and-career/foundations-development-program": {
      "title": "The Foundations Development Program",
      "description": "The Foundations Development Program | Sabancı Üniversitesi Header Top Menu Career My SU Alumni Site içinde ara Hızlı Bağlantılar Hakkımızda TR EN Site içinde ara Hızlı Bağlantılar Hakkımızda TR EN Ana gezinti menüsü About University About Sabancı University Our Philosophy and Goals Our Policies and Documents Rules and Regulations Gender Equality Action Plan Kalite Güvence ve Strateji Kurulu Kurum Değerlendirme Raporları Sustainability Administrative Units and Boards Board of Trustees University Management Directors International Board of Overseers Distinguished Research Fellows Student Union Our Academic Principles Academic Freedom and Integrity Scientific and Applied Research Misconduct Non Discrimination Statement Sexual Harassment Policy Statement Domestic Violence Prevention and Support Statement Academic Faculties and Programs Starting Out School of Languages Faculty of Engineering and Natural Sciences Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences Sabancı Business School All Programs Academic Calendar Support for Education and Career The Foundations Development Program (TGP) Student with Special Needs Support Unit (SSN) Civic Involvement Projects (CIP) Executive Development Unit (EDU) Career & Intership Office Exchange Programs University Registration, Scholarships and Fees Student Resources Scholarships & Tuition Fees Registration Information F.A.Q Research Research Strategy and Management Research Strategy Research Management Ankara Project Office Research Development and Technology Transfer Office (SUATT) Research Planning and Policy Development Office Research Opportunities Centers and Forums Laboratories Information Center Processes Researchers Industry For Entrepreneurs For Students Research Outputs and Performance Research Highlights Patents & Technologies Research Output & Performance University Rankings Araştırma Videoları Campus Food, Drink and Accommodation Food & Beverage Dormitories Faculty Housing Sports, Culture and Art Sport Activities Culture & Arts Events Sabancı University Performing Arts Center (SGM) Health and Safety Medical Center Security Services Business and Environment Safety Campus and City Natural Life on Campus Campus Plan Life in Istanbul Admission Admission Prospective Undergraduate Students Graduate Programs International Student External Transfer and Vertical Transfer Special Student Communication Communication Bilgi Edinme Başvurusu Communication Center Service Providers Social Media Telephone and Addresses Transport Campus Shuttle Schedule Transportation to Campus by Car İ.E.T.T. Bus Schedule Sabancı University Altunizade Digital Campus Karaköy Minerva Han Communication Center Transportation Services Quick Links Quick Links News From Sabancı University (Newsletter) Graduate Programs Support Vacant Positions ELAE Announcements Duyurular ELAE Sınav Duyuruları YKS Kayıt İşlemleri Lisansüstü Başvuru Dökümanları ve Gereklilikler Kurumlara Arası Yatay Geçiş Başvuruları Quick Links Career My SU Alumni Breadcrumb Home Academic Support for Education and Career The Foundations Development Program (TGP) The Foundations Development Program The Foundations Development Program A tool for individuals who are curious, competent and believe in universality. Core training program design. The Foundations Development Program What is the Foundation Development Program? The Foundation Development Program consists of two important educational phases: the Foundation Development Year (FYY) and the University Courses that form our core curriculum, which all Sabancı University students must complete regardless of their program selection and specialization preferences. First Year University Courses Detail First Year University Course Registration Detail Exemption Detail The Foundations Development Program University Courses The Foundations Development Program consists of two important educational stages, Foundations Development Year (FDY) and the University Courses that constitute a mandatory core-curriculum for all Sabancı University students irrespective of their choice of program specialisation. During FDY a condense English education program is performed, starting from basic, intermediate and upper-intermediate levels. FDY language courses and the related exams are offered by the School of Languages. To gain exemption from FDY, students should be successful in English Language Assessment Exam (ELAE) or Exemption Exams from the FDY. Students who gain FDY exemption become freshmen. All freshman courses are University Courses, there are also some other University Courses in later years of instruction. The Freshman University Courses which have to be taken by freshman students are one of the fundamental elements supporting the structure of our interdisciplinary approach in the absence of traditional departments. This mandatory core-curriculum structure introduces students the basics of science, academic skills, and knowledge about the world around them that would not only equip them for the challenges of the future but would also lay the foundations of an interdisciplinary approach that will be necessary in their faculty courses and informed choice of specialisation. What are the University Courses? Students who complete the Foundation Development Year (FDY) or who are eligible to skip through FDY continue their studies in the freshmen year. University Courses are the totality of courses obligatory for every student enrolled at Sabanci University to complete starting at freshmen level and throughout their bachelors. University Courses constitute the core of education at Sabanci University and aim to build a foundation conducive to follow faculty courses, to develop the practice of critical thinking with respect to ethical and moral problems, to get to know more thoroughly the society students currently live in, the world at large, and themselves. Natural Sciences, Social Sciences and sub-fields related to these sciences are all combined in university courses which are thereby designed in a way to guide students in choosing their major program of study. University Courses consist of the following course groups: Freshmen Year University Courses: These courses are automatically registered to the schedule of the student. Major Works Courses: Starting with the incoming students of 2015, FENS students must take one, FASS and FMAN students take two from the pool of these courses. Upon the completion of prerequisites, students can take these courses whenever they prefer. Project Course: This is required only to students who entered the Sabanci University after 2017-18 Academic Year. The students have to take this course on freshman or sophomore year. Law and Ethics course: All students must take this course. Upon the completion of prerequisites, students can take these courses whenever they prefer. Freshman Courses Course Code Course Name SU Credits ECTS AL 102 Academic Literacies 3 5 HIST 191 Principles of Atatürk and the History of the Turkish Revolution I 2 3 HIST 192 Principles of Atatürk and the History of the Turkish Revolution II 2 3 IF 100 Computational Approaches to Problem Solving 3 5 MATH 101 Calculus I 3 6 MATH 102 Calculus II 3 6 NS 101 Science of Nature I 4 6 NS 102 Science of Nature II 4 6 SPS 101 Humanity and Society I 3 6 SPS 102 Humanity and Society II 3 6 TLL 101 Turkish Language and Literature I 2 3 TLL 102 Turkish Language and Literature II 2 3 CIP 101N Civic Involvement Projects I 0 1 Major Works Courses Course Code Course Name SU Credits ECTS HUM 201 Major Works of Literature 3 5 HUM 202 Major Works of Western Art 3 5 HUM 207 Major Works of Western Philosophy 3 5 HUM 311 Major Works of Literature: The World Before Modernity 3 5 HUM 312 Major Works of Modern Art 3 5 HUM 317 Major Works of Moral Philosophy 3 5 HUM 321 Major Works of Literature: The Modern World 3 5 HUM 322 Major Works of Art: The World Before Modernity 3 5 HUM 371 Major Works of Literature: The Islamic World 3 5 Project Course Course Code Course Name SU Credits ECTS PROJ 201 Undergraduate Project Course 1 1 Law and Ethics Course Course Code Course Name SU Credits ECTS SPS 303 Law and Ethics 3 5 Taking these courses helped me become better equipped to deal with world affairs, thus giving me specific perspectives that I can discuss with different people and which I now support. HAGAR FADDA He describes his experience with the Foundation Development Program Experiences of Our Other Students The development and success of our students We are determined to support. Our staff Öğretim Üyeleri Research Assistants Emeritus Faculty Members Visiting Faculty Members Accessibility Tool Navigation Adjustment Hide Images Screen and Text Reader Content Settings Cursor Enlarge the cursor and change its color. White Black Font Sizing Increase and decrease the font size. - + Text Magnifier Contrast Image  Description Abc Dyslexia Font Reading Guide Stop Animation Clear Selections Dipnot İhale İlanları KVKK Aydınlatma Metni Gizlilik Bildirimi Orta Mahalle, 34956 Tuzla, İstanbul, Türkiye Telefon: +90 216 483 90 00 Fax: +90 216 483 90 05 © Sabancı Üniversitesi 2023 Play All"
