      "title": "Student with Special Needs Support Unit (SSN)",
      "description": "Student with Special Needs Support Unit (SSN) | Sabancı Üniversitesi Header Top Menu Career My SU Alumni Site içinde ara Hızlı Bağlantılar Hakkımızda TR EN Site içinde ara Hızlı Bağlantılar Hakkımızda TR EN Ana gezinti menüsü About University About Sabancı University Our Philosophy and Goals Our Policies and Documents Rules and Regulations Gender Equality Action Plan Kalite Güvence ve Strateji Kurulu Kurum Değerlendirme Raporları Sustainability Administrative Units and Boards Board of Trustees University Management Directors International Board of Overseers Distinguished Research Fellows Student Union Our Academic Principles Academic Freedom and Integrity Scientific and Applied Research Misconduct Non Discrimination Statement Sexual Harassment Policy Statement Domestic Violence Prevention and Support Statement Academic Faculties and Programs Starting Out School of Languages Faculty of Engineering and Natural Sciences Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences Sabancı Business School All Programs Academic Calendar Support for Education and Career The Foundations Development Program (TGP) Student with Special Needs Support Unit (SSN) Civic Involvement Projects (CIP) Executive Development Unit (EDU) Career & Intership Office Exchange Programs University Registration, Scholarships and Fees Student Resources Scholarships & Tuition Fees Registration Information F.A.Q Research Research Strategy and Management Research Strategy Research Management Ankara Project Office Research Development and Technology Transfer Office (SUATT) Research Planning and Policy Development Office Research Opportunities Centers and Forums Laboratories Information Center Processes Researchers Industry For Entrepreneurs For Students Research Outputs and Performance Research Highlights Patents & Technologies Research Output & Performance University Rankings Araştırma Videoları Campus Food, Drink and Accommodation Food & Beverage Dormitories Faculty Housing Sports, Culture and Art Sport Activities Culture & Arts Events Sabancı University Performing Arts Center (SGM) Health and Safety Medical Center Security Services Business and Environment Safety Campus and City Natural Life on Campus Campus Plan Life in Istanbul Admission Admission Prospective Undergraduate Students Graduate Programs International Student External Transfer and Vertical Transfer Special Student Communication Communication Bilgi Edinme Başvurusu Communication Center Service Providers Social Media Telephone and Addresses Transport Campus Shuttle Schedule Transportation to Campus by Car İ.E.T.T. Bus Schedule Sabancı University Altunizade Digital Campus Karaköy Minerva Han Communication Center Transportation Services Quick Links Quick Links News From Sabancı University (Newsletter) Graduate Programs Support Vacant Positions ELAE Announcements Duyurular ELAE Sınav Duyuruları YKS Kayıt İşlemleri Lisansüstü Başvuru Dökümanları ve Gereklilikler Kurumlara Arası Yatay Geçiş Başvuruları Quick Links Career My SU Alumni Breadcrumb Home Academic Support for Education and Career Student with Special Needs Support Unit (SSN) Student with Special Needs Support Unit (SSN) Every Student Deserves Equal Opportunity We are here to help you overcome the barriers you may encounter throughout your university life. As the Special Needs Student Support Unit, we work to ensure that you can access the support you need in academic life, on campus, and in social settings. Together, we assess your needs, plan appropriate accommodations, and help make your university experience more accessible. Abouts Us Why Does This Unit Exist? At Sabancı University, we believe that every student should be able to reach their full potential. For our students with special needs, equal access is not an exception—it is a fundamental right and one of our priorities. By fully complying with the regulations of the Council of Higher Education (YÖK) and going beyond minimum requirements, we have established a comprehensive support network that covers physical accessibility, examination accommodations, counseling services, psychological support, and more. Who Can Apply? Students experiencing any of the following conditions are encouraged to apply: Physical disabilities Visual impairments Hearing impairments Chronic health conditions Learning disabilities ADHD (Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder) Surgery, injury, or temporary health conditions Other special needs that may affect academic life If you are unsure whether your situation qualifies, you are still welcome to contact us. How Can We Support You? Academic Accommodations Extended exam time, separate examination rooms, and specialized learning materials. Campus Accessibility Coordination of physical accessibility arrangements, transportation support, and campus access solutions. Individual Guidance and Support One-on-one support, guidance, and follow-up throughout your academic journey. Referral Services Coordinated referrals to Psychotherapy Services, the Health Center, and other relevant university units. Confidentiality and Your Rights The information you share with us is kept confidential. Your information will not be shared without your explicit consent. Only the accommodations necessary for academic arrangements are communicated to faculty members. Your health information and personal data are protected. You remain an active participant in all decisions regarding your support process. Frequently Asked Questions Questions on Your Mind Who can apply? Any Sabancı University student with a permanent or temporary disability, health condition, or special need that affects their academic life may apply. What documents are required? In most cases, a current medical report, specialist evaluation report, or other official documentation is required. Additional documents or information may be requested when necessary. How are academic accommodations determined? Every student's needs are unique. Appropriate accommodations are determined collaboratively based on your documentation and individual consultations. Will my instructors learn about my medical condition? No. Your diagnosis and medical information are not shared. Faculty members are only informed about the accommodations necessary to support your academic participation. Will my information remain confidential? Yes. All information and documentation are handled in accordance with confidentiality principles and data protection regulations. Can I receive support for temporary health conditions? Yes. Students whose academic life is affected by surgery, injury, or temporary health conditions may also request support. How long can I continue receiving support? You may continue to receive support from our unit throughout your studies for as long as your needs persist. Your support plan can be reviewed and updated when necessary. Ready to Apply? Completing the application form takes only a few minutes. After submitting your form and supporting documents via email, we will contact you as soon as possible. Download Application Form Click Here to Download Contact Us Student Resources specialneeds@sabanciuniv.edu Monday – Friday | 09:00 – 16:30 🕒 Monday - Friday | 09:00 – 16:30 If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact us by email. Accessibility Tool Navigation Adjustment Hide Images Screen and Text Reader Content Settings Cursor Enlarge the cursor and change its color. White Black Font Sizing Increase and decrease the font size. - + Text Magnifier Contrast Image  Description Abc Dyslexia Font Reading Guide Stop Animation Clear Selections Dipnot İhale İlanları KVKK Aydınlatma Metni Gizlilik Bildirimi Orta Mahalle, 34956 Tuzla, İstanbul, Türkiye Telefon: +90 216 483 90 00 Fax: +90 216 483 90 05 © Sabancı Üniversitesi 2023 Play All"
    },
