Culture & Arts Events Sabancı University Performing Arts Center (SGM) Health and Safety Medical Center Security Services Business and Environment Safety Campus and City Natural Life on Campus Campus Plan Life in Istanbul Admission Admission Prospective Undergraduate Students Graduate Programs International Student External Transfer and Vertical Transfer Special Student Communication Communication Bilgi Edinme Başvurusu Communication Center Service Providers Social Media Telephone and Addresses Transport Campus Shuttle Schedule Transportation to Campus by Car İ.E.T.T. Bus Schedule Sabancı University Altunizade Digital Campus Karaköy Minerva Han Communication Center Transportation Services Quick Links Quick Links News From Sabancı University (Newsletter) Graduate Programs Support Vacant Positions ELAE Announcements Duyurular ELAE Sınav Duyuruları YKS Kayıt İşlemleri Lisansüstü Başvuru Dökümanları ve Gereklilikler Kurumlara Arası Yatay Geçiş Başvuruları Quick Links Career My SU Alumni Breadcrumb Home Academic Support for Education and Career Civic Involvement Projects (CIP) Civic Involvement Projects (CIP) The Civic Involvement Projects (CIP 101) course has been a compulsory requirement for all Sabancı University students since 1999. Civic Involvement Projects provide an educational program that aims to promote and implement participatory democracy among individuals. Through this course, students are introduced to the concept of active citizenship and engage in a learning process based on experience rather than theoretical knowledge. As part of Sabancı University’s core curriculum, Civic Involvement Projects aim to raise students’ awareness of their communities and encourage them to act with a sense of social responsibility, enabling them to make a difference while fulfilling their duties to society. Links CIP Web Sitesi Accessibility Tool Navigation Adjustment Hide Images Screen and Text Reader Content Settings Cursor Enlarge the cursor and change its color. White Bla